[{:db/id "q-357534/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "1a64e558-bdfc-54d4-b715-b1c1ead3b056" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-357534/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "759852d6-a263-5474-85d9-b1d10f4e3858" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-357534/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-357534/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-357534" :question/id #uuid "73d18dc8-cd5c-5b83-a157-8a5bb955ecb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-357534" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/d15f201b8f2a8521c68321b9ce15e5b13091fc899728822526d11cdcee08a393.png)\n\nThe total area $A$ of the region between the curve $y=2-\\frac{6}{x+1}$ and the $x$-axis from $x=1$ to $x=5$ is given by the following integral expression below: \n\n$$\nA=-\\,{\\int }_{1}^{a}(2-\\frac{6}{x+1})\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{a}^{5}(2-\\frac{6}{x+1})\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To determine the missing limit of integration, we need to find the $x$-intercept of the curve $y=2-\\frac{6}{x+1}.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-\\frac{6}{x+1} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{6}{x+1} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{6}{x+1} & =2 \\\\ 6 & =2(x+1) \\\\ 6 & =2x+2 \\\\ 4 & =2x \\\\ 2 & =x \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only solution between $x=1$ and $x=5$ is $x=2.$\n\nSince $2\\in [1,5],$ we have two regions:\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=1$ to $x=2.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=2$ to $x=5.$\n\nSo, $a=2$ and the final expression will be\n\n$$\nA=\\,-\\,{\\int }_{1}^{2}(2-\\frac{6}{x+1})\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{5}(2-\\frac{6}{x+1})\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-357534/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18cd52a9-1524-5099-b1d8-858345328bad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-357534"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73894/selection/82ec26c0001ae04b27cd2a63ab6318b183a710f05feb55d071b767b49c260b88" :answer/id #uuid "9f1b77f2-9fa2-5b00-9921-6376ec5b2646" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73894/selection/c2223b402abc62f38e0912260502c4886959d43580edcea4b6bfd37e37b0f72b" :answer/id #uuid "3030c4cd-bab7-5aae-b08c-723657732924" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73894/selection/03a4102f13ad3e0ac65ab53676c3f89cede3c650c4dd4e31a2b43a62847e184f" :answer/id #uuid "ce1d5a79-1f1d-5ab3-b19b-d041b1f032c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73894/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "ff6998ad-e7bf-582e-abaa-78858771f494" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73894/selection/c6aee8d6d50719f300760eb2495148ceeb4788aba7a3722d82e109afb19d07de" :answer/id #uuid "345be7ed-e390-5f5c-8f1f-dcc6f8d311aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73894/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4d86218-b45e-505b-a154-8b9972eacb3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73894/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-73894/selection/82ec26c0001ae04b27cd2a63ab6318b183a710f05feb55d071b767b49c260b88" "q-73894/selection/c2223b402abc62f38e0912260502c4886959d43580edcea4b6bfd37e37b0f72b" "q-73894/selection/03a4102f13ad3e0ac65ab53676c3f89cede3c650c4dd4e31a2b43a62847e184f" "q-73894/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-73894/selection/c6aee8d6d50719f300760eb2495148ceeb4788aba7a3722d82e109afb19d07de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73894" :question/id #uuid "6fa85593-213a-592b-beaa-a7478f15ea2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73894" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/0e0466f463644e25cd2a615c445b6b32a6d9ae236c44658609cd778c5222fcae.png)\n\nThe total area $A$ of the region between the curve $y={x}^{2}+3x$ and the $x$-axis from $x=-4$ to $x=-1$ is given by the integral expression below. What is the value of $a?$\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-4}^{a}({x}^{2}+3x)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{a}^{-1}({x}^{2}+3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To determine the missing limit of integration, we need to find the $x$-intercept of the curve $y={x}^{2}+3x.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}+3x \\\\ 0 & ={x}^{2}+3x \\\\ x(x+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $x=0$ or $x=-3.$ The only solution between $x=-4$ and $x=-1$ is $x=-3.$\n\nSince $-3\\in [-4,-1]$, we have two regions:\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-4$ to $x=-3.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-3$ to $x=-1.$\n\nSo, $a=-3$ and the final expression will be\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-4}^{-3}({x}^{2}+3x)\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}({x}^{2}+3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73894/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18cd52a9-1524-5099-b1d8-858345328bad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73894"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-357547/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "d29c6d55-65fb-5b20-be6d-c65c2067662b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-357547/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "13b2acf1-35f1-52d5-bd44-7bbbbb259979" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-357547/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-357547/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-357547" :question/id #uuid "f1dc5fba-db36-5ec7-9733-135e3c16f8ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-357547" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/196dcb953e409bd1688e77661e4a635aa92b7edb837f26bb2666592b3ff54a90.png)\n\nThe total area $A$ of the region between the curve $y=2-\\frac{8}{x-1}$ and the $x$-axis from $x=3$ to $x=9$ is given by the following integral expression below: \n\n$$\nA=-\\,{\\int }_{3}^{a}(2-\\frac{8}{x-1})\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{a}^{9}(2-\\frac{8}{x-1})\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To determine the missing limit of integration, we need to find the $x$-intercept of the curve $y=2-\\frac{8}{x-1}.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-\\frac{8}{x-1} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{8}{x-1} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{8}{x-1} & =2 \\\\ 8 & =2(x-1) \\\\ 8 & =2x-2 \\\\ 10 & =2x \\\\ 5 & =x \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only solution between $x=3$ and $x=9$ is $x=5.$\n\nSince $5\\in [3,9],$ we have two regions:\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=3$ to $x=5.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=5$ to $x=9.$\n\nSo, $a=5$ and the final expression will be\n\n$$\nA=-\\,{\\int }_{3}^{5}(2-\\frac{8}{x-1})\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{5}^{9}(2-\\frac{8}{x-1})\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-357547/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18cd52a9-1524-5099-b1d8-858345328bad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-357547"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140583/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "83debc0f-a54e-50b6-8253-d055daf32990" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140583/selection/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4" :answer/id #uuid "faae2241-f8c5-555c-979a-2cb9c7680ff4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140583/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "228b8630-a226-5e47-9395-aa0f19cfbbe4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140583/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer/id #uuid "07aff3d5-7c97-5eb0-8817-53946ffabc16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140583/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "e1493a3c-f7dc-54b8-8267-14a0cc6f05ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140583/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6af2fec3-d336-5a2e-a5dc-355674a680ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140583/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-140583/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-140583/selection/ed43d5224151224cedff9572a0bc31a320bd7a8ebd2aa526ca5884904c9d6cb4" "q-140583/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-140583/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" "q-140583/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140583" :question/id #uuid "cb68cdd3-2757-5be6-bde1-043b15f42f06" :question/math-academy-id "q-140583" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/8b729d243b344df6b26757773bf0521dea80da34fc727541d24babd3732563cf.png)\n\nThe total area $A$ of the region between the curve $y=4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}$ and the $x$-axis from $x=-1$ to $x=\\frac{5}{2}$ is given by the integral expression below. What is the value of $a?$\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-1}^{a}(4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4})\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{a}^{5/2}(4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4})\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To determine the missing limit of integration, we need to find the $x$-intercept of the curve $y=4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4} & =-4 \\\\ {x}^{4} & =16 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{{x}^{4}} & =\\pm \\sqrt[4]{16} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt[4]{{2}^{4}} \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only solution between $x=-1$ and $x=\\frac{5}{2}$ is $x=2.$\n\nSince $2\\in [-1,\\frac{5}{2}],$ we have two regions:\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-1$ to $x=2.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=2$ to $x=\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nSo, $a=2$ and the final expression will be\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-1}^{2}(4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4})\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{5/2}(4-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4})\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140583/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18cd52a9-1524-5099-b1d8-858345328bad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140581/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer/id #uuid "459f2dde-d054-5eba-b913-f53e1bfdab1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140581/selection/7627fb02fec1c7a865cb3e7797f7ea7835cb8ec3423f266885f8f5d01084e358" :answer/id #uuid "ede24615-890c-5f2d-a307-83092da199ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140581/selection/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" :answer/id #uuid "31b0ad8a-59d4-502e-b07e-2da476398e7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140581/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "4c26869c-1d5b-578d-a78c-d6387fbf5ec2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140581/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "909dac4a-0462-5aa6-9cf0-2de7b09052fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140581/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0266ad0-eaa3-5d36-96b3-eb24756d22a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140581/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-140581/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" "q-140581/selection/7627fb02fec1c7a865cb3e7797f7ea7835cb8ec3423f266885f8f5d01084e358" "q-140581/selection/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" "q-140581/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-140581/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140581" :question/id #uuid "45513b5f-8d07-55fb-b016-242a9220da80" :question/math-academy-id "q-140581" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/72ecb00845c906fd44da9b5f559fb06445b3d8ac154064743fd433cc895e1916.png)\n\nThe total area $A$ of the region between the curve $y=\\frac{4}{x-2}+1$ and the $x$-axis from $x=-5$ to $x=0$ is given by the integral expression below. What is the value of $a?$\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-5}^{a}(\\frac{4}{x-2}+1)\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{a}^{0}(\\frac{4}{x-2}+1)\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To determine the missing limit of integration, we need to find the $x$-intercept of the curve $y=\\frac{4}{x-2}+1.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{x-2}+1 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{x-2} & =-1 \\\\ 4 & =-(x-2) \\\\ 4 & =-x+2 \\\\ 2 & =-x \\\\ x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-2\\in [-5,0],$ we have two regions:\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-5$ to $x=-2.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-2$ to $x=0.$\n\nSo, $a=-2$ and the final expression will be\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-5}^{-2}(\\frac{4}{x-2}+1)\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-2}^{0}(\\frac{4}{x-2}+1)\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140581/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "18cd52a9-1524-5099-b1d8-858345328bad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140581"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-74159/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "7d343799-240d-5c2e-b84a-d70fa18f470d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74159/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "45f130ba-4d5c-5d21-9cfd-195f8b9c2100" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74159/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "563ce85a-ceda-5ca1-a319-6e987a4ea69e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74159/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "c09106a6-2515-5d39-990e-fc6c1a26a54b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74159/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "d7e57acb-0a3d-526e-b419-4572e35d7dcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74159/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6016ad9d-51b1-5a37-8bf1-cea1e22acebb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74159/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-74159/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-74159/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-74159/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-74159/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-74159/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74159" :question/id #uuid "8778f441-1732-5187-8111-f3ff261a56d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-74159" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/cd6555800f4b7c7a7ae76ef9dd75ebca543ea4898b4205dd24df15f52f95653d.png)\n\nFind the total area of the region between the curve $y=-4{x}^{3}$ and the $x$-axis from $x=-1$ to $x=1,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $0\\in [-1,1]$, we have two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-1$ to $x=0$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=1.$\n\nFor $x\\in [-1,0]$, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}-4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the region for $x\\in [0,1]$ lies completely below the $x$-axis.  Hence, the value of\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{1}-4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwill be negative. Therefore, the area that we want is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}-4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(1-0) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total area is\n\n$$\nA={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=1+1=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-74159/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "262a1469-0920-565f-9268-28f0e5f1faf5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74159"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-54475"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/14bd6415062b5e08f183e22059cffa2893442c87c391dfdb1c020c942e15af83.png)\n\nFind the total area of the region between the curve $y=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}$ and the $x$-axis from $x=-1$ to $x=1,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $0\\in [-1,1]$, we have two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-1$ to $x=0.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=1.$\n\nNotice that the region for $x\\in [-1,0]$ lies completely below the $x$-axis. Hence, the value of\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwill be negative. Therefore, the area that we want is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (0-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x\\in [0,1],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total area is\n\n$$\nA={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-345648/field-1/2682fec702d3cff1f75a5b0eb4c92d85859f9802e7e2712c4698da1b77df3e37" :answer/id #uuid "98d04d2a-5c95-5704-88ea-89c5cf1ba279" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{59}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345648/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a11e841-0208-5397-8e02-5eb9498c7153" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345648/field-1/2682fec702d3cff1f75a5b0eb4c92d85859f9802e7e2712c4698da1b77df3e37" :answer-field/choices ["q-345648/field-1/2682fec702d3cff1f75a5b0eb4c92d85859f9802e7e2712c4698da1b77df3e37"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345648" :question/id #uuid "7b4f6bab-5693-558e-9353-a41ddaa8a4fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-345648" :question/problem "Find the total area $A$ of the region between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}+6x-5$ and the $x$-axis from $x=2$ to $x=7.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+6x-5 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x+5 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)(x-5) & =0 \\\\ x & =1,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $5\\in [2,7],$ we have two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=2$ to $x=5.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=5$ to $x=7.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/e14a891e924a6911a0df962dc5c5b41c90b0c411de4ebe1f7e52ec1953e4124c.png)\n\nNotice that the region for $x\\in [5,7]$ lies completely below the $x$-axis. Hence, the value of\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{5}^{7}(-{x}^{2}+6x-5)\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwill be negative.\n\nTherefore, the area that we want is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}(-{x}^{2}+6x-5)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{2}^{5}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+6{\\int }_{2}^{5}x\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{2}^{5}+3{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{2}^{5}-5x\\,{|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[{5}^{3}-{2}^{3}]+3[{5}^{2}-{2}^{2}]-5[5-2] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(125-8)+3(25-4)-5(3) \\\\  & =-\\frac{117}{3}+63-15 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x\\in [5,7],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =-{\\int }_{5}^{7}(-{x}^{2}+6x-5)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{5}^{7}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-6{\\int }_{5}^{7}x\\,\\text{d}x+5{\\int }_{5}^{7}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{5}^{7}-3{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{5}^{7}+5x\\,{|}_{5}^{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[{7}^{3}-{5}^{3}]-3[{7}^{2}-{5}^{2}]+5[7-5] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(343-125)-3(49-25)+5(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{218}{3}-72+10 \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =9+\\frac{32}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{59}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-345648/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "262a1469-0920-565f-9268-28f0e5f1faf5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345648"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140607/selection/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b" :answer/id #uuid "851b8d15-e643-5dfc-8f51-7600fceb69f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140607/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "2c9b71c7-fb50-5939-bfb9-4a1cf9fee847" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140607/selection/49b9ee464914b05da889b24a56e026e479c6989f8c7fb611b2828c3fa7d40d87" :answer/id #uuid "f173af9d-93ac-5140-8b17-fc43fd9897af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{31}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140607/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" :answer/id #uuid "a26599e3-3036-5269-a448-d4835ab4f30f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140607/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "8914a5ed-60a1-5eb6-bda7-1b540193e6ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140607/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b3b77c4-8650-5b8e-9d4d-e082e4e1f5cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140607/selection/49b9ee464914b05da889b24a56e026e479c6989f8c7fb611b2828c3fa7d40d87" :answer-field/choices ["q-140607/selection/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b" "q-140607/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-140607/selection/49b9ee464914b05da889b24a56e026e479c6989f8c7fb611b2828c3fa7d40d87" "q-140607/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" "q-140607/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140607" :question/id #uuid "301d1a57-9f93-5f8f-9e49-7d0812255410" :question/math-academy-id "q-140607" :question/problem "Find the total area of the region between the curve $y=3x-{x}^{2}$ and the $x$-axis from $x=1$ to $x=4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x(3-x) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $3\\in [1,4],$ we have two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=1$ to $x=3.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=3$ to $x=4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/219d7aa5b976c97d47a96d0c94c3d61d139d5ddddc55b82d0df68f19ad6d5149.png)\n\nNotice that the region for $x\\in [3,4]$ lies completely below the $x$-axis. Hence, the value of\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{3}^{4}(3x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwill be negative. Therefore, the area that we want is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(3x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[{3}^{2}-{1}^{2}]-\\frac{1}{3}[{3}^{3}-{1}^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[9-1]-\\frac{1}{3}[27-1] \\\\  & =12-\\frac{26}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x\\in [3,4],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =-{\\int }_{3}^{4}(3x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{3}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{4}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{3}^{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[{4}^{2}-{3}^{2}]+\\frac{1}{3}[{4}^{3}-{3}^{3}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}[16-9]+\\frac{1}{3}[64-27] \\\\  & =-\\frac{21}{2}+\\frac{37}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total area is\n\n$$\nA={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=\\frac{10}{3}+\\frac{11}{6}=\\frac{31}{6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-140607/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "262a1469-0920-565f-9268-28f0e5f1faf5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140607"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140603/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" :answer/id #uuid "89a4e94e-8c72-5c00-8bbb-554821877634" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140603/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "0ac92ec0-12e1-5ba5-b21c-c69dfd7c1d24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140603/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "3dc3b00e-4a1f-5cb2-9ac1-ab210dbffb33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140603/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "e37df24d-095d-5ef8-9088-c0c9b252d63f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140603/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "4c2e8d4a-650f-5f14-9205-123ea32bbb1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140603/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2fe25926-3c90-52d9-a3e9-a4ef9d256019" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140603/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer-field/choices ["q-140603/selection/9ab64b945e95c1c3798cea70f4ae7ad55133b01b9b894848e70b56c91ffbae97" "q-140603/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-140603/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" "q-140603/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-140603/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140603" :question/id #uuid "b41d7f47-1b5b-51dc-95a6-fdbed5217147" :question/math-academy-id "q-140603" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/2ffa9585853d1230c9664a27dffcd832aec5cdff3fa1d3f01c9012d2835d101e.png)\n\nFind the total area of the region between the curve $y={x}^{2}-2x$ and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=3,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x & =0 \\\\ x(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2\\in [0,3],$ we have two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=2.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=2$ to $x=3.$\n\nNotice that the region for $x\\in [0,2]$ lies completely below the $x$-axis. Hence, the value of\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwill be negative. Therefore, the area that we want is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =-{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}+{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[{2}^{3}-{0}^{3}]+[{2}^{2}-{0}^{2}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[8-0]+4 \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x\\in [2,3],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}({x}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{2}^{3}-{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[{3}^{3}-{2}^{3}]-[{3}^{2}-{2}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[27-8]-[9-4] \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{3}-5 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total area is\n\n$$\nA={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{4}{3}=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140603/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "262a1469-0920-565f-9268-28f0e5f1faf5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140603"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117444/selection/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" :answer/id #uuid "86e0f3bb-a919-5c9e-846c-ba85fe50be31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "90" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117444/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "b5ae8a9e-6bab-5c58-92d6-e82afeb52477" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117444/selection/d6944c4d51ee6e8916d5e2815a8478bad91a2f9e9e9bcd499b503b9fbcb165ab" :answer/id #uuid "dbdbad80-28c1-5c6d-a963-c4a7259772d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117444/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" :answer/id #uuid "990159cf-470b-51d9-ae0d-f7586d10cf2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117444/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "c4e88a54-b3f1-5628-9b04-951bdd579407" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117444/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c29c4e6d-63ed-5496-a693-48945e416661" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117444/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" :answer-field/choices ["q-117444/selection/f9ce6d2531e925e028befc33f5bb5202bf5c98dc29df5818c58d5bd59c914412" "q-117444/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-117444/selection/d6944c4d51ee6e8916d5e2815a8478bad91a2f9e9e9bcd499b503b9fbcb165ab" "q-117444/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" "q-117444/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117444" :question/id #uuid "a268e040-4834-5a95-a543-76ff2c8ba400" :question/math-academy-id "q-117444" :question/problem "Find the total area of the region between the curve $y=9-{x}^{2}$ and the $x$-axis from $x=-3$ to $x=6.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (x-3)(x+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=-3$ and $x=3$ are our real solutions. Since $3\\in [-3,6]$, we have two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-3$ to $x=3.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=3$ to $x=6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/70df9534ea4f69993871888a5f751ecd6aea9d1e0aaaf128d55442d9913b3dd5.png)\n\nFor $x\\in [-3,3]$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{3}(9-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9x{|}_{-3}^{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{-3}^{3} \\\\  & =[9(3)-9(-3)]-[\\frac{(3)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(-3)^{3}}{3}] \\\\  & =54-18 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that for $x\\in [3,6]$ the region lies completely below the $x$-axis. Hence, the value of\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-3}^{6}(9-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwill be negative. Therefore, the area that we want is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =-{\\int }_{-3}^{6}(9-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-9{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{6}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-9x{|}_{3}^{6}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{3}^{6} \\\\  & =-9[6-3]+[\\frac{(6)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(3)^{3}}{3}] \\\\  & =-27+63 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total area is\n\n$$\nA={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=36+36=72.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117444/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d89ba41-6d24-548a-bd97-66830b752ba9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117444"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117447/selection/f1a3f6364b4b6488166c92c743a5a8e2e2bdb28aff5bc6025ac2678cb4926932" :answer/id #uuid "3a0e610b-f861-5df6-b456-cd6bb20b88f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "200" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117447/selection/16943fbe431b8ad65062bb7a8cd5d2f82696bba5ae52194b653416a034b2e8e1" :answer/id #uuid "15a8692b-da92-55cf-8d1a-43af6efac442" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "152" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117447/selection/16ad0c2afac2310ac4213e4c147a8ff875d80d039203f9a4d0bd13914017aaff" :answer/id #uuid "2f90d268-0b81-582c-aeb7-b685427ea03a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "104" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117447/selection/56c57502ed9362f3f416b4398e79545a0252f6594946b2d60ff940ea8bef1e7b" :answer/id #uuid "6bcde9cf-9530-504f-b793-5fe928fc95e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "44" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117447/selection/c5fad6b1da11b9b990be9e0d2fcb83dfa156d8e05ce4b7ef6802ba6bbc66674b" :answer/id #uuid "6886b8ff-c220-56be-933d-05baddf578d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "98" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117447/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1df80af9-b3b5-5383-acb9-154d01d89fed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117447/selection/16943fbe431b8ad65062bb7a8cd5d2f82696bba5ae52194b653416a034b2e8e1" :answer-field/choices ["q-117447/selection/f1a3f6364b4b6488166c92c743a5a8e2e2bdb28aff5bc6025ac2678cb4926932" "q-117447/selection/16943fbe431b8ad65062bb7a8cd5d2f82696bba5ae52194b653416a034b2e8e1" "q-117447/selection/16ad0c2afac2310ac4213e4c147a8ff875d80d039203f9a4d0bd13914017aaff" "q-117447/selection/56c57502ed9362f3f416b4398e79545a0252f6594946b2d60ff940ea8bef1e7b" "q-117447/selection/c5fad6b1da11b9b990be9e0d2fcb83dfa156d8e05ce4b7ef6802ba6bbc66674b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117447" :question/id #uuid "e9345a33-4d56-54d6-be3b-08ac569073ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-117447" :question/problem "Find the total area of the region between the curve $y=27-3{x}^{2}$ and the $x$-axis from $x=-3$ to $x=5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27-3{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & =27 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=-3$ and $x=3$ are our real solutions. Since $3\\in [-3,5]$, we have two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-3$ to $x=3.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=3$ to $x=5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/6b3ca7be487585b296aaeb0b3fa7eb4ce8b9b4f9ad35d52baefa04f2fbbed621.png)\n\nFor $x\\in [-3,3]$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{3}(27-3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =27{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{-3}^{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =27x{|}_{-3}^{3}-{x}^{3}{|}_{-3}^{3} \\\\  & =27[3-(-3)]-[(3)^{3}-(-3)^{3}] \\\\  & =162-54 \\\\  & =108.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that for $x\\in [3,5]$ the region lies completely below the $x$-axis. Hence, the value of\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{3}^{5}(27-3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwill be negative. Therefore, the area that we want is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =-{\\int }_{3}^{5}(27-3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-27{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{3}^{5}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-27x{|}_{3}^{5}+{x}^{3}{|}_{3}^{5} \\\\  & =-27[5-3]+[(5)^{3}-(3)^{3}] \\\\  & =-54+98 \\\\  & =44.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total area is\n\n$$\nA={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=108+44=152.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117447/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d89ba41-6d24-548a-bd97-66830b752ba9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117447"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-54522/selection/481403949dbe33872059d395862de40801147c5dad3c54f02674ace2f7c4225f" :answer/id #uuid "6a2bfd6f-1051-58e2-ac3a-0c126a13ebf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}-({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54522/selection/57028d0996da9d2a9cc693c19b66eb08a80b382520617dcf63cd3eb701bb3fde" :answer/id #uuid "986d2e1e-a68a-505e-a53c-4d502a46863e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54522/selection/76703620343170cd06e942c33cd3dfdc1dbe35cb6f315ae2d8d0f9fce897bbc5" :answer/id #uuid "06ddef86-df53-5ce7-812e-8b5c330a2d86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}-({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54522/selection/c451665baea50d24875032bb9e2955ae34934e2f0073db6fb10346abe42e971b" :answer/id #uuid "1b49e458-c29d-5d10-908b-d866be2853a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54522/selection/0efb949171b353a3ed3ea5afeb1862525b65f4c85885269f1dcef61a70019ff6" :answer/id #uuid "ca92b6da-0030-54d0-a7e3-e1d6208fc941" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}-({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54522/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "41ad1c55-7472-5426-b6fe-79b2851b5eea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-54522/selection/481403949dbe33872059d395862de40801147c5dad3c54f02674ace2f7c4225f" :answer-field/choices ["q-54522/selection/481403949dbe33872059d395862de40801147c5dad3c54f02674ace2f7c4225f" "q-54522/selection/57028d0996da9d2a9cc693c19b66eb08a80b382520617dcf63cd3eb701bb3fde" "q-54522/selection/76703620343170cd06e942c33cd3dfdc1dbe35cb6f315ae2d8d0f9fce897bbc5" "q-54522/selection/c451665baea50d24875032bb9e2955ae34934e2f0073db6fb10346abe42e971b" "q-54522/selection/0efb949171b353a3ed3ea5afeb1862525b65f4c85885269f1dcef61a70019ff6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-54522" :question/id #uuid "684f1c1d-407b-5f72-a75f-8a2754804ac2" :question/math-academy-id "q-54522" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/7ffd75051b71a3b8665ac68418ff24dac2124a6b7ff50633a0a5843df9cff196.png)\n\nWhich integral expression gives the total area enclosed between the curve $y={x}^{5}-x$ and the $x$-axis, as shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we the limits of integration. We find the $x$-intercepts of the curve as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}-x & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{4}-1) & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}-1)({x}^{2}+1) & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ x(x-1)(x+1) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $x=\\pm 1$ or $x=0.$ \nThis gives us two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-1$ to $x=0.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=1.$\n\nFor $x\\in [-1,0]$, we have\n\n$$\n{A}_{1}={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNotice that for $x\\in [0,1]$ the region lies completely below the $x$-axis. Hence, the value of\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwill be negative. Therefore, the area that we want is given by\n\n$$\n{A}_{2}=-{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{1}-({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, the total area is\n\n$$\nA={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}-({x}^{5}-x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-54522/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d89ba41-6d24-548a-bd97-66830b752ba9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-54522"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140577/selection/4dd966d679683feb50997e8352eec9dfba4fde18d893addef4881e20ed512039" :answer/id #uuid "8f242e50-4cc4-5e48-bd0a-8ed3e285d9ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}-({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140577/selection/9d0f47735603cf08247d6ed0ed357a32b617258ee9b2ce30b6becc374635a711" :answer/id #uuid "483b8021-c9ec-5ff5-9217-2fc0295e8dcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140577/selection/c466fe80a8289d152ff630052187de28eea797cab0abc1a403ff844484cf5064" :answer/id #uuid "2d5dbc85-1098-56e5-b0fe-bffbea04ba12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{3}({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140577/selection/0c374e31db50fca37ecde8281723fcbf1de4158e76f570eff9f8880c4be6c2d5" :answer/id #uuid "aec6f29d-4780-59bb-9dc3-e188508ccca1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}-({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140577/selection/5bc7df54b96d88f4645f8d04e645a271ac80c6e7408a6f7372fa36ed084912ce" :answer/id #uuid "ec5d54ff-4f07-5fba-98e3-fd63638ad29c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}-({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140577/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fabd73f9-e194-5bf3-8afd-e8ab191e56cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140577/selection/4dd966d679683feb50997e8352eec9dfba4fde18d893addef4881e20ed512039" :answer-field/choices ["q-140577/selection/4dd966d679683feb50997e8352eec9dfba4fde18d893addef4881e20ed512039" "q-140577/selection/9d0f47735603cf08247d6ed0ed357a32b617258ee9b2ce30b6becc374635a711" "q-140577/selection/c466fe80a8289d152ff630052187de28eea797cab0abc1a403ff844484cf5064" "q-140577/selection/0c374e31db50fca37ecde8281723fcbf1de4158e76f570eff9f8880c4be6c2d5" "q-140577/selection/5bc7df54b96d88f4645f8d04e645a271ac80c6e7408a6f7372fa36ed084912ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140577" :question/id #uuid "76bf4b59-f550-57f6-94a7-13de4968da86" :question/math-academy-id "q-140577" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/a4871287696f20009bd7d2b8793965c9f68e35faa4ad150477643f1d3ec77e38.png)\n\nWhich integral expression gives the total area enclosed between the curve $y={x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}$ and the $x$-axis, as shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limits of integration. We find the $x$-intercepts of the curve as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}({x}^{2}-x-6) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}(x+2)(x-3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $x=-2,x=0$ or $x=3.$ Since $0\\in [-2,3],$ we have two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-2$ to $x=0.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=3.$\n\nFor $x\\in [-2,0]$, we have\n\n$$\n{A}_{1}={\\int }_{-2}^{0}({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNotice that for $x\\in [0,3]$ the region lies completely below the $x$-axis. Hence, the value of\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwill be negative. Therefore, the area that we want is given by\n\n$$\n{A}_{2}=-{\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{3}-({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, the total area is\n\n$$\nA={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}={\\int }_{-2}^{0}({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}-({x}^{5}-{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140577/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d89ba41-6d24-548a-bd97-66830b752ba9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140577"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140580/selection/4c4c55688c576a505436823a209e694bfc782b9bc39b71eb6f9647c7e40abccb" :answer/id #uuid "0907a60f-77db-55fb-9a04-873a8468d7dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{3}-(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140580/selection/6c9cfc114a04339e4b5b0d8977caf0b63e0ed387463082fc41d311fc77db0510" :answer/id #uuid "0f34b53a-c56a-55fa-83f9-459de0404f97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}-(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140580/selection/9913ae7abcfd73a30cab8fbd986df29f3ca08ed6477858a240e92451818f3792" :answer/id #uuid "186befc6-b17a-5940-9c9b-92671bcb5ccb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-9}^{9}(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140580/selection/d1f9fe4447792652ede906bf4e8991bfd139c88cbe17121250767f0a90e04d4b" :answer/id #uuid "70862a02-0575-5652-9e74-eff10065bff9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-9}^{0}-(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{9}(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140580/selection/2b5b470f35ae024da74c1aa2e4b4074cadf64de3cf54ce07b6e25e8b376de1fb" :answer/id #uuid "3bdd6d6a-1542-57ab-b9c5-dd95d94723b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{0}(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}-(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140580/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5c73f82-8cda-5fba-955d-bd50cbdf26c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140580/selection/6c9cfc114a04339e4b5b0d8977caf0b63e0ed387463082fc41d311fc77db0510" :answer-field/choices ["q-140580/selection/4c4c55688c576a505436823a209e694bfc782b9bc39b71eb6f9647c7e40abccb" "q-140580/selection/6c9cfc114a04339e4b5b0d8977caf0b63e0ed387463082fc41d311fc77db0510" "q-140580/selection/9913ae7abcfd73a30cab8fbd986df29f3ca08ed6477858a240e92451818f3792" "q-140580/selection/d1f9fe4447792652ede906bf4e8991bfd139c88cbe17121250767f0a90e04d4b" "q-140580/selection/2b5b470f35ae024da74c1aa2e4b4074cadf64de3cf54ce07b6e25e8b376de1fb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140580" :question/id #uuid "d7e31157-b1fc-52ce-8aec-355690d5bd82" :question/math-academy-id "q-140580" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/2a32d95d98a2c2cefe08b492c368a99df61a8cc3a1f66018a6dfe444e65146b8.png)\n\nWhich integral expression gives the total area enclosed between the curve $y=9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5}$ and the $x$-axis, as shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the limits of integration. We find the $x$-intercepts of the curve as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}(9-{x}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}(3-x)(3+x) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $x=\\pm 3$ or $x=0.$ Since $0\\in [-3,3],$ we have two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-3$ to $x=0.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=3.$\n\nNotice that for $x\\in [-3,0]$ the region lies completely below the $x$-axis. Hence, the value of\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-3}^{0}(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwill be negative. Therefore, the area that we want is given by\n\n$$\n{A}_{2}=-{\\int }_{-3}^{0}(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-3}^{0}-(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor $x\\in [0,3]$, we have\n\n$$\n{A}_{2}={\\int }_{0}^{3}(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, the total area is\n\n$$\nA={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}={\\int }_{-3}^{0}-(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}(9{x}^{3}-{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140580/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d89ba41-6d24-548a-bd97-66830b752ba9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140580"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3888"] :question/problem "The total area $A$ of the region between the curve $y=x^3-1$ and the $x$-axis from $x=-2$ to $x=2$ is given by the integral expression below. What is the value of $a?$\n\n$$\nA = \\displaystyle -\\int_{-2}^{a} (x^3-1) \\:\\textrm{d}x + \\int_{a}^{2} (x^3-1) \\:\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/57d01ea60e3cd9770f2ef978e46e2cef7b69a9fcdc2ac478d5b6c73d8f366c7b.png)" :question/worked-solution "To determine the missing limit of integration, we need to find the $x$-intercept of the curve $y=x^3-1.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{3}-1 \\\\ (0) & ={x}^{3}-1 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =1 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $1 \\in [-2,2]$, we have two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-2$ to $x={\\color{blue}{1}}.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x={\\color{blue}{1}}$ to $x=2.$\n\nSo, $a={\\color{blue}1}$ and the final expression will be\n\n$$\nA = \\displaystyle -\\int_{-2}^{\\color{blue}1} (x^3-1) \\:\\textrm{d}x + \\int_{\\color{blue}1}^{2} (x^3-1) \\:\\textrm{d}x.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3887"] :question/problem "Find the total area of the region between the curve $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}x^3$ and the $x$-axis from $x=-1$ to $x=\\dfrac{3}{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/0d3ede3cfbec765228ea184c74e0cb35f1df2a9340bd1cb703a0990249fecf30.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $0 \\in \\left[-1,\\dfrac{3}{2}\\right]$, we have two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-1$ to $x=0.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=\\dfrac{3}{2}.$\n\nNotice that for $x \\in  [-1,0]$ the region lies completely below the $x$-axis. Hence, the value of\n\n$$\n\\int_{a}^{b} y(x) \\:\\textrm{d}x = \\int_{-1}^{0}  \\dfrac{x^3}{2}  \\:\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nwill be negative. Therefore, the area that we want is given by\n\n$$\nA_1 = -\\int_{-1}^{0}  \\dfrac{x^3}{2}  \\:\\textrm{d}x .\n$$\n\nFor $x \\in\\left[0,\\dfrac{3}{2}\\right]$, we have\n\n$$\nA_2 = \\int_{0}^{3/2}\\dfrac{x^3}{2} \\:\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nThe total area is\n\n$$\nA = A_1+A_2 = - \\int_{-1}^{0} \\dfrac{x^3}{2}  \\:\\textrm{d}x + \\int_{0}^{3/2} \\dfrac{x^3}{2}  \\:\\textrm{d}x .\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3/2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{8}]}_{-1}^{0}+{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{8}]}_{0}^{3/2} \\\\  & =-[0-\\frac{1}{8}]+[\\frac{81}{128}-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{81}{128} \\\\  & =\\frac{97}{128}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3889"] :question/problem "Find the total area of the region between the curve $y=x^3-9x$ and the $x$-axis from $x=-3$ to $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-9x & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}-9) & =0 \\\\ x(x-3)(x+3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=0,$ $x=-3,$ and $x=3$ are our real solutions. Since $0 \\in [-3,3]$, we have two regions: \n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=-3$ to $x=0.$\n\n- The area between the curve and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013598/assets/29a51c9892de59037e84bace2f8b5822222c3056a05af861cbd741390a437a61.png)\n\nFor $x \\in [-3,0]$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}({x}^{3}-9x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-9{\\int }_{-3}^{0}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}{|}_{-3}^{0}-\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{-3}^{0} \\\\  & =[0-\\frac{(-3)^{4}}{4}]-9[0-\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{2}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{81}{4}+\\frac{81}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that for $x \\in [0,3]$ the region lies completely below the $x$-axis. Hence, the value of\n\n$$\n\\int_{a}^{b} y(x) \\:\\textrm{d}x = \\int_{0}^{3} \\left(x^3-9x\\right) \\:\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nwill be negative. Therefore, the area that we want is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =-{\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{3}-9x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+9{\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}{|}_{0}^{3}+\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =-[\\frac{(3)^{4}}{4}-0]+9[\\frac{(3)^{2}}{2}-0] \\\\  & =-\\frac{81}{4}+\\frac{81}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total area is\n\n$$\nA = A_1+A_2 =  \\dfrac{81}{4} + \\dfrac{81}{4} = \\dfrac{81}{2}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
